          "Do not treat 58% as a stable majority: a 58-42 result with a fractured 2024 primary outcome leaves this district open to a credible challenger if the incumbent neglects the 42% or fails to deliver on education and infrastructure priorities that both homeowners and renters evaluate annually.",
